---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { companyPolicies, policySourceIndex } from "../../data/policies";
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const linked=companyPolicies.filter(p=>p.link);
const empty=companyPolicies.find(p=>!p.link);
---
<BaseLayout title="Company policies & Group Policy" description="Seven Group Policy objects in Nova Corp: what each one sets, where it is linked, and what I tested." breadcrumbs={[{label:"Map",href:"map/"},{label:"Workstation rules"}]}>
<section class="page-head"><div class="container">
<div class="eyebrow">Identity / Group Policy</div>
<h1>I set a rule once. Did it reach the right person?</h1>
<p class="lead" style="margin-top:18px">Nova Corp sets passwords, workstation security, wallpaper and mapped drives with Group Policy. Each policy is linked to a part of the directory. Open one to see what it sets and what I tested.</p>
<div class="button-row" style="margin-top:24px">
<a class="btn" href={base+"policies/contractor-usb/"}>Follow the contractor restriction →</a>
<a class="btn ghost" href={base+"directory/"}>Open the directory</a>
</div>
</div></section>
<section class="section compact"><div class="container">
<div class="stats-strip" style="margin-bottom:32px">
<div class="stat"><b>{companyPolicies.length}</b><span>Policies in the lab</span></div>
<div class="stat"><b>{linked.length}</b><span>Linked, not enforced</span></div>
<div class="stat"><b>1</b><span>Empty and unlinked</span></div>
</div>
<div class="paper panel" style="margin-bottom:30px">
 <p class="kicker">Three questions, three kinds of proof</p>
 <div class="proof-grid">
  <div><strong>1. Configured</strong><p>What is saved in the policy?</p></div>
  <div><strong>2. Linked</strong><p>Which domain or OU gets it?</p></div>
  <div><strong>3. Tested</strong><p>Did a real account or workstation process it, and did the rule work?</p></div>
 </div>
 <p class="muted" style="margin-top:18px">A link does not prove the policy was applied. A <code>gpresult</code> entry does not prove a USB drive was refused.</p>
</div>
<div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">The seven policies</div><h2>Policies linked to the company</h2></div><a class="text-link" href={policySourceIndex}>Source records ↗</a></div>
<div class="card-list">
 {linked.map(p=><a class="system-card" href={base+"policies/"+p.slug+"/"}>
  <small>{p.side} settings · Link enabled, not enforced</small>
  <h3>{p.name}</h3><p>{p.summary}</p>
  <p class="tag-line"><span class="mini-badge">Linked to {p.link?.label}</span></p>
  <span class="readmore">See the settings and what I tested →</span>
 </a>)}
</div>
{empty&&<div class="paper panel" style="margin-top:28px">
 <p class="kicker">Recorded but not deployed</p>
 <h3 style="margin:11px 0">{empty.name}</h3>
 <p class="muted">The keyboard policy exists but has no settings and no link. I found keyboard preferences in the Domain Controllers policy instead.</p>
 <a class="evidence-link" href={base+"policies/"+empty.slug+"/"}>See why it does nothing →</a>
</div>}
<div class="note" style="margin-top:26px">I exported all seven policies. Each one lets Authenticated Users apply it. Who actually gets it still depends on the link, inheritance and filtering.</div>
</div></section>
</BaseLayout>
